  "plain_text": "THE FUTURE EMERGENT: EVENTSThroughout the six weeks of the exhibition we have many events planned and will continue to add events throughout the month! VIRTUAL OPENING\n​\n​\nThe Afrofuture is Now where Black Futures Matter: Artists Speak on Imagining Radical Possibilities for a World on Fire\n​\n​\n​\nSaturday July 11, 5 PM RSVP & LINKS\nThe Future Emergent: Only from new words can new worlds emerge\n​\nThis live reading event featuring artists Alicia Escott, Ari Kalinoswki, Connie Zheng, and Serena JV Elston, part of The Future Emergent exhibition, will give you a unique insight into the work in which they live the unimaginable and seek radical possibility for the future.\nthursday August 13,\n6:30PM-8PM\n​ RSVP & LINKS\nThe Afrofuture is Now: Black & BIPOC Immersive storytelling, Art & Gaming\n​\n​\nImagining Radical Possibilities in Black & BIPOC Immersive storytelling, art and gaming our way out of Climate and Covid-19 superthreats.\n​\n​\n​\nSaturday August 1,\n5PM-6:30PM\n​ RSVP & LINKS\nBlack Speculative Word and Poetry in Motion\n​\n​\nJoin us in conversation with poets Dera Williams, Anna White, Thaddeus Howze, Vernon Keeve III and facilitated by Lonny Avi Brooks as they read, perform and time travel summoning fierce, resilient Black Speculative visions into motion.\n​\nFriday August 14,\n7PM-8:30PM\n​ RSVP & LINKS\nDIGITAL DOULAS\nART CAMP\n​\n​\n​\nA digital exploration of layers, worlds and possibilities and creation of a new space for the future with Judit Navratil\n​\n​\nMonday August 3, 6PM RSVP & LINKS\nLinDSay TuNkl\n​\n​\n​\n​\nA guttural noise making and embodied movement workshop: join us and wail.\n​\n​\n​\ntuesday August 11,\n12PM-2PM\n​ RSVP & LINKS",
